<div class="sop-meta">
  <div><strong>Trigger</strong> Discovery call ends with "let's do it" or "send me something"</div>
  <div><strong>Owner</strong> Lead owner</div>
  <div><strong>Time</strong> 30-45 min to draft + send</div>
  <div><strong>Output</strong> Signed agreement returned, kickoff scheduled</div>
</div>

<h2>Proposal structure</h2>
<p>Keep it under one page. PDFs printed at 600 dpi nobody reads. Plain Markdown email or a Notion-style doc both work; same content either way.</p>

<ol>
  <li><strong>What you have today.</strong> One paragraph reflecting what I heard on the call. Builds trust by mirroring their words.</li>
  <li><strong>What I will build.</strong> Bullet list of pages + features + the operational pages they're already getting. Specific page names, not abstract counts.</li>
  <li><strong>What's NOT in scope.</strong> Reference <a href="/what-we-build/#review">what-we-build / what's NOT included</a> directly.</li>
  <li><strong>Timeline.</strong> Date ranges, not "weeks." "Discovery to design preview: April 30 - May 7. Build: May 7 - May 21. Launch window: May 22-28."</li>
  <li><strong>Investment.</strong> Lump-sum number or monthly + length. No surprise add-ons; if there's a setup fee, list it.</li>
  <li><strong>How to start.</strong> One link: the agreement, ready to sign. Don't make them email back to ask for it.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Pricing positioning</h2>
<p>Two plans, not three. Keep the choice simple.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Monthly Care Plan</strong> &middot; $175/mo, $0 down, 12-month minimum, then month-to-month with 30-day notice.</li>
  <li><strong>Lump-Sum</strong> &middot; $4,000 one-time, up to 10 content pages, code ownership transferred on delivery. Optional $50/mo hosting; content updates billed at $150/hour.</li>
</ul>
<p>The default recommendation is the monthly plan unless they specifically asked for ownership. If you have to choose for them: monthly. It's the better deal long-term and the better experience for the client.</p>

<h2>Steps</h2>

<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Open the proposal template in Notion / Google Docs.</li>
  <li>Fill in their business name, the discovery-call summary, the page list.</li>
  <li>Pick monthly vs. lump-sum based on what they signaled.</li>
  <li>Add a one-line agreement link at the bottom: <code>https://pikespeakwebdesigns.com/agreement/</code>.</li>
  <li>Send via email with a short cover note. CC nobody.</li>
  <li>Set a 7-day reminder. If no response, send one polite follow-up. After that, close as "soft-no."</li>
  <li>When they sign: confirm receipt within 1 business hour. Schedule the kickoff call. Move to <a href="/sop/onboarding/">phase 04</a>.</li>
</ul>

