<h2>Common issues</h2>

<div class="sop-callout sop-callout--warn">
  <strong>They negotiate the price</strong>
  I do not discount the monthly plan. I can shorten the term (no), drop a service (yes, take a page off and remove a feature), or recommend the lump-sum option if they want a smaller commitment.
</div>

<div class="sop-callout sop-callout--warn">
  <strong>They want a custom contract / their lawyer to review</strong>
  Fine. Send the published agreement at <code>/agreement/</code> as the starting point. Hard "no" on indemnification + IP-transfer clauses outside the existing terms; almost everything else is negotiable within reason. If their lawyer takes more than two weeks, the project goes on hold.
</div>

<div class="sop-callout sop-callout--warn">
  <strong>They want a 50% discount for a 24-month commitment</strong>
  No. Our model is no-discount, no-deposit. Stay disciplined.
</div>

<div class="sop-callout">
  <strong>They sign but the kickoff call is 4+ weeks out</strong>
  OK. Note the start date in CRM, send the onboarding link, and let them fill out at leisure. I do not start the build until the kickoff happens.
</div>

<h2>Exit criteria</h2>
<p>Agreement signed and on file (PDF in the project Drive folder). Kickoff call on the calendar. Onboarding form link sent. Proceed to <a href="/sop/onboarding/">phase 04</a>.</p>
